{
	"id": "effect-shows-errors",
	"text": "Here is the Effect version of slowDie. It still gets a random number, takes a non-blocking, 1 second nap, and then returns the result. Let's make it lethal. If the roll is 4, we will fail with our trusty VeryBadRoll. And finally, we have a type error! The error type propagates from Effect.fail to the surrounding effect. We are forced to reckon with it. Welcome to TypeScript.",
	"code": "\nconst slowDie: Effect.Effect<number> = Effect.gen(function* () {\n  const n = yield* Random.nextIntBetween(1, 7)\n  yield* Effect.sleep(\"1 second\")\n  return n\n})",
